    "Unrelated product/Python changes preserve bindings; compiler/ABI/QEMU/Ninja/CMake changes invalidate them. A changed tier3 implementation dependency preserves the identities of its predecessors.",
    "Contract validation executes the existing scoped toolchain report verifier and checks the original SDK report hashes. All upstream stages authenticate the expected predecessor; later stages also authenticate the contract report used for patchelf.",
    "Mocked producer dispatch tests execute real policy loading and report-binding paths, checking host-tool identities, explicit executor arguments, all five triplets, schema2 output and legacy SDK schema1 compatibility.",
    "Complete SDK checker independently derives the scoped vcpkg policy from current release and records report bytes; the legacy path requires exact release identity and rejects unsupported/mixed formats and unsafe files.",
    "Actual Bake graphs omit full release/schema/renderers from all five vcpkg roots. Their entrypoints load with exactly six copied runtime modules; the input reader loads the full tier3 policy from only three modules and seventeen projections.",
    "Packaging copies release at its own stage boundary. The final SDK checker operates using only the scripts explicitly copied by its Docker stage."
